// @emit-error a function value may not take a nullable or map parameter
// @hint Intentionally-unused parameter
// The NICHE half of the un-annotated nullable lambda-param pin
// (`closure-nullable-param-lambda-pin.vl`), on a payload with NO `$fnsig` token at all.
//
// `emitClosureValueCore`'s floor is `cloSigKeyExt(fe) == ""`: a function VALUE whose
// env-leading signature has no interned `$fnsig` cannot be soundly called as a value, so the
// call site would fall back to the all-i32 arity functype and `call_indirect` at the WRONG
// type. Which payloads reach that floor is decided by ONE table — `repSigTokOfKind`, the
// canonical kind→token character:
//
//   * the nullable-REF niches WITH a token — `string | null` (`N`), `S | null` (`n<slot>;`),
//     `i32[] | null` (`o`) — are in the ABI at the param position as well as the result one,
//     and are simply correct (`closure-value-nullable-niche-param.vl` runs all three);
//   * the four DISTINCT-BACKING scalar-list niches (`f64[] | null` here, and the `i64[]` /
//     `f32[]` / `string[]` twins), `S[] | null` and `{[string]: V} | null` have no token
//     character, so their key stays "" and this floor is what the program gets;
//   * the BOXED payloads (`i32|null`, `i64|null`, `f64|null`, `f32|null`) rep as the value-
//     union box and never came near the floor.
//
// So this file pins the floor ITSELF — that a payload outside the token table is a CLEAN
// REJECT rather than invalid wasm — and the token table is what decides its membership. It
// carries the param's OWN type rather than borrowing a shared alias precisely because that
// membership is per-payload.
//
// The un-annotated form reaches the floor only because `synthParamAnnots` pins the real
// nullable onto the parameter. Without that pin the param kept the i32 default, an i32
// parameter keys a perfectly ordinary `$fnsig`, the key was NON-EMPTY, the floor stayed
// silent, and the call site pushed the raw ref into an i32 parameter: `vl check` rc=0 and a
// module that could not instantiate ("type mismatch: expected i32, found (ref $type)").
//
// ONE RESIDUAL, measured and deliberately left: a RECURSIVE nullable
// (`type L = {v: i32, n: L | null}`; `const f: (L | null) => i32 = (_k) => 1`) is still
// invalid wasm. `tyToEmitName`'s cycle guard returns "" for a cyclic type — a recursive type
// has no finite structural render — so the pin declines and the param keeps the i32 default.
// That is the RENDERER's back-edge vocabulary, not the pin's arm, so it is a separate root:
// the fix there is a nominal spelling for the recursive shape, which every other consumer of
// that renderer would want too.

const f: (f64[] | null) => i32 = (_k) => 1
print(f(null))
